{
  "about": "Run, in order, by the desktop's real service.ts (with its search index stubbed; apps/web/scripts/ios-conformance-fixtures.test.ts) and by the Swift NoteStore (StoreConformanceTests.swift) against the same starting database, which the TypeScript builds with the real repos. After every step both record the result and every row of notes, groups, notebooks, trashed_notes, trashed_groups and sqlite_sequence; the two must match. The start: notebooks 1 (Notebook), 2 (Work), 3 (Archive); groups 1 Projects (nb 2), 2 Sub (in 1), 3 Deep (in 2), 4 Loose, 5 Empty, 6 Second, 7 Third (4 to 7 top level in nb 1); notes 1 Alpha (tags x,y), 2 Beta (in 1), 3 Gamma (in 2), 4 Delta (in 3), 5 Epsilon (in 4), 6 Zeta, 7 Eta, 8 Theta, 9 Iota (in 4), 10 Kappa (in 4), 11 Work note (nb 2, ungrouped). 'at' is the clock for the step (the TypeScript sets it; Swift passes it). A uuid not in the start database is compared as 'new'. An error is recorded by kind: notFound, invalidGroupMove, groupNotEmpty, lastNotebook, notebookNotEmpty, noNotebooks.",
